flick-tiler (1.3) trixie; urgency=medium

  * New command floating list|add|remove PATTERN: the apps that always
    float (Float=), used by the Settings window (flickos-control). The
    status JSON also has the main window width (ratio).
  * New command gap N (pixels, 0-64) for the Settings window; the status
    JSON also has the gap.

 -- Jon <dvbondoy@gmail.com>  Tue, 22 Sep 2026 20:18:13 +0800

flick-tiler (1.2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * The daemon runs for the whole session again, as in 1.0: autostart
    starts it at login whether tiling is on or off, turning tiling off
    only drops the fragment, and no daemon is started on demand. The
    hint about windows that stay floating now comes when tiling is
    turned on. Unchanged from 1.1: one daemon per session (daemon.lock),
    a fragment left by a daemon that died is cleared, and the panel
    button is updated with SIGRTMIN+8.

 -- Jon <dvbondoy@gmail.com>  Sun, 20 Sep 2026 07:49:52 +0800

flick-tiler (1.1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * The daemon runs only while tiling is on: at login it exits at once
    if tiling is off, flick-tiler on (Super+T, the panel button) starts
    it, and it exits when tiling is turned off. A lock keeps it to one
    daemon. A fragment left by a daemon that died is removed. The panel
    button is updated with SIGRTMIN+8 instead of a status --follow
    process. Depends on flickos-layouts (>= 1.8).
  * Turning tiling on while windows are open shows a notification: they
    stay floating until tiled with Super+Shift+T.

 -- Jon <dvbondoy@gmail.com>  Sat, 19 Sep 2026 08:41:52 +0800

